# Extending

How to add a source, a column, a view or a page, and which version to change, so that nothing goes stale. The
design behind each part is in [the architecture](../design/architecture.md). How to test it is in
[testing](testing.md). Add a section here for each kind of change that this app makes often.

## A new source, or a change in a source's format

1. Describe how the source is read in practice in `docs/sources/<source>.md`, and add it to the index
   ([docs/README.md](../README.md)).
2. Add or change the reader in `src/{{ package }}/ingest/`, with a test on a small made-up file. The test writes it
   to a temporary folder (`tmp_path`), or keeps it in `tests/data/` when it is bigger. Never use a real one.
3. Run `uv run {{ project_name }} ingest` (`/ingest`), then `uv run {{ project_name }} status`.

## A schema change
{% if backup %}
Run `uv run {{ project_name }} backup` before the change.
{% endif %}
1. Change `src/{{ package }}/db/schema.sql`, with a comment on each new column.
2. A table that holds data the sources can't give again needs a migration in `src/{{ package }}/db/store.py`: add
   it to `MIGRATIONS` (it brings version N to N + 1), and raise `SCHEMA_VERSION` by one. Without the new version,
   the migration never runs. Otherwise, make the database again{% if curations %} (`/rebuild-database`){% endif %}.

## A contract change

The browser app reads only the contract's views ([the contract](../design/contract.md)).

1. Change the view in `src/{{ package }}/db/schema.sql` and in the reference schema,
   `src/{{ package }}/contract/schema.sql`.
2. Change the version in `src/{{ package }}/contract/__init__.py`: the minor version for a new view or column, the
   major version for a removed or changed one.
3. Update [the contract](../design/contract.md): a test checks it against the schema.

## A page of the app

1. Add the page in `src/{{ package }}/app/`, reading only the contract views.
2. Add its questions to [the dashboard](../design/dashboard.md), and its checks to
   [the browser checks](../design/browser-checks.md).
3. Walk the checks with `/app-check`.
{%- if curations %}

## A new kind of decision

1. Add the table in `src/{{ package }}/db/schema.sql`, and a `CuratedTable` for it in `src/{{ package }}/curated.py`.
2. Every command that changes it runs inside `curating()`, which writes `curated/` after it.
3. Describe the file in `curated/README.md`.
{%- endif %}
